# The busybox applets in the gate's image (gate.Dockerfile), in place of GNU's coreutils,
# findutils, grep, sed, gawk, diffutils, tar and util-linux's flock: what contrib/ccs-receive,
# contrib/ccs-backup-receive, contrib/docker/web/init and the web compose's healthchecks run
# (awk: frontmatter.awk and ccs-front-bash's markdown.awk on the same awk the backend runs them on), plus
# chown, cp, install and ls for tests/gate.sh, so it runs against exactly what ships; readlink, diff, ln and sync for
# the site built here (contrib/gate-build, ccs-front-bash, lib/images.sh and common.sh). Nothing else
# is compiled into busybox.
awk
basename
cat
chmod
chown
cmp
comm
cp
cut
date
diff
dirname
du
find
flock
grep
head
install
ln
ls
mkdir
mktemp
mv
readlink
rm
rmdir
sed
sha256sum
sleep
sort
stat
sync
tail
tar
test
timeout
touch
tr
wc
xargs
# and the options of theirs named otherwise than CONFIG_FEATURE_<APPLET>_* (which each applet's
# line turns on): head -c (the alerts, the backup receiver), tail -c, du -m (the backup receiver)
CONFIG_FEATURE_FANCY_HEAD
CONFIG_FEATURE_FANCY_TAIL
CONFIG_FEATURE_HUMAN_READABLE
